cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the specific software version. Add the Zenodo-assigned DOI after
  archival; no DOI has been minted yet.
title: 'Cosmic Futures Laboratory: a numerical laboratory for conditional cosmological futures'
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-05'
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Karatum
    given-names: Mustafa
abstract: >-
  An interactive FLRW background simulator with adaptive numerical integration,
  conservative dark-matter transfers, conditional asymptotic continuation,
  astrophysical tracer approximations, uncertainty sampling and versioned
  observational provenance. A research software preview, not a unique forecast
  of the actual cosmic fate or an externally peer-reviewed solver.
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - FLRW
  - dark energy
  - numerical simulation
  - reproducibility
  - scientific visualization
references:
  - type: article
    title: 'Planck 2018 results. VI. Cosmological parameters'
    authors:
      - name: Planck Collaboration
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1051/0004-6361/201833910
  - type: article
    title: 'A Dying Universe: The Long-Term Fate and Evolution of Astrophysical Objects'
    authors:
      - family-names: Adams
        given-names: Fred C.
      - family-names: Laughlin
        given-names: Gregory
    year: 1997
    doi: 10.1103/RevModPhys.69.337
